## 3. Architecture and Technical Specifications

### 3.1 Magnet Cross‑Section (Textual Drawing)

The magnet is a stack of 12 double‑pancake coils, each wound with 145 turns of 12 mm‑wide, 15‑filament striated REBCO tape. The inner radius of the winding pack is \(R_i = 5.0\;\text{mm}\). The outer radius of the bare coil is \(R_o = 28.0\;\text{mm}\). The axial height is \(H = 35\;\text{mm}\).

On top of the coil, a 6 mm‑thick glass‑fibre/epoxy overband is wound with a radially increasing fibre volume fraction. The inner overband radius is 28.0 mm; the outer overband radius is 34.0 mm. The fibre fraction varies from 22 % at the inner surface to 30.4 % at the outer surface.

Four independent superconducting shim coils are wound as thin solenoids at fixed radii outside the overband. Their axial positions and numbers of turns are chosen to generate orthogonal \(P_2\), \(P_4\), and \(P_6\) field corrections. The shim coils are made from narrow (2 mm) REBCO tape and operate at currents below 20 A.

The entire assembly fits inside a cylindrical cryostat with an outer diameter of 68 mm. The warm bore is 10 mm. Thermal radiation shields and a two‑stage cryocooler maintain the coil at 20 K. The winding tension is applied during fabrication by a controlled‑stress winding machine and verified by strain gauges on the overband.

