## 4. Optimization Implementation and Results

### 4.1 Surrogate Training and NSGA‑II Configuration

A Latin hypercube sample of 320 design points was evaluated with the full coupled FEM model (H‑formulation + mechanics + thermal). A multi‑output Gaussian process with Matérn 5/2 kernel was trained on these data. The NSGA‑II was run with population size 200 for 150 generations, using the GP posterior mean for fitness evaluation. The adaptive operator schedule and SA acceptance were applied as described. Hypervolume convergence to \(10^{-5}\) tolerance was achieved at generation 132.

### 4.2 Pareto Front and Selected Design

The final Pareto front contains 43 non‑dominated solutions. The design chosen for Phase‑3 lies at the knee of the homogeneity–buildability trade‑off. Its full FEM verification yielded the specifications in Table 3.2. The homogeneity GP prediction was 0.92 ppm with posterior \(\sigma = 0.08\;\text{ppm}\); the FEM value was 0.94 ppm, within the 95 % confidence interval.

### 4.3 Adjoint Optimization of Pre‑Emphasis

The waveform optimization was run with 20 control points and \(\lambda = 10^{-4}\). L‑BFGS converged in 34 iterations to a final gradient norm of \(2\times10^{-6}\). The optimised waveform features an initial overshoot of 12 %, a dwell at peak current of 180 s, and a smooth exponential tail. Forward FEM verification with this waveform gave a drift of 0.0078 ppm/h over 3600 s.

