Using the definition in Appendix A.8 and the normalisation described there, the buildability score for the Phase‑3 design is \(\mathcal{B}=0.91\), corresponding to a very low predicted failure probability under the assumed tolerance distribution. The score is insensitive to the contact resistivity because of the constant‑\(\rho_{ct}\) approach.

